---
import { instants, records } from './model.mjs';
interface Props { advanced?: boolean }
const { advanced = false } = Astro.props;
const id = advanced ? 'two-clocks' : 'effective-price';
---
<figure class="history-figure" data-price-figure data-advanced={String(advanced)} aria-labelledby={`${id}-title`}>
  <figcaption id={`${id}-title`}><span class="figure-number">Figure {advanced ? '3' : '2'}</span> {advanced ? 'The same business day, two recorded accounts' : 'A scheduled price is not yet today’s price'}</figcaption>
  <div class="history-scene">
    <div class="history-options">
      <label>Price effective at
        <select data-effective aria-label={`Price effective at, figure ${advanced ? '3' : '2'}`}>
          {instants.map((instant, i) => <option value={String(i)} selected={i === 2}>{advanced || i === 0 ? instant.label : instant.label.split(' · ')[0]}</option>)}
        </select>
      </label>
      {advanced && <label>According to the record at
        <select data-recorded aria-label="According to the record at">
          {records.map((record, i) => <option value={String(i)}>{record.label}</option>)}
        </select>
      </label>}
    </div>
    <p class="time-key">Effective time → <span>All dates October 2026, UTC. The drawing shows 20–23 October.</span></p>
    <div class="date-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>20 Oct</span><span>21 Oct</span><span>22 Oct</span><span>23</span></div>
    <div class="clock-band" data-band="0">
      <p class="band-label">Recorded from 21 Oct 12:00 {advanced && <span>until 24 Oct 09:00</span>}</p>
      <div class="time-strip">
        <div class="price-span" data-assertion="1" style="width:66.6667%"><span>A1</span><strong>20.00</strong><span>before 22 Oct</span></div>
        <div class="price-span" data-assertion="2" style="width:33.3333%"><span>A2</span><strong>22.00</strong><span>from 22 Oct →</span></div>
        <span class="time-marker" data-marker aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>
    </div>
    {advanced && <div class="clock-band" data-band="1">
      <p class="band-label">Recorded from 24 Oct 09:00 <span>onwards</span></p>
      <div class="time-strip">
        <div class="price-span" data-assertion="3" style="width:33.3333%"><span>A3</span><strong>20.00</strong><span>before 21 Oct</span></div>
        <div class="price-span" data-assertion="4" style="width:66.6667%"><span>A4</span><strong>22.00</strong><span>from 21 Oct →</span></div>
        <span class="time-marker" data-marker aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>
    </div>}
    <p class="price-result" data-live><span>Selected price</span> <strong data-price>20.00</strong> <span data-match>A1</span></p>
    <p class="history-explanation" data-price-explanation aria-live="polite" data-live>At 21 Oct 12:00 the selected account still gives 20.00. Its 22.00 version starts at 22 Oct 00:00.</p>
    <p class="agreement-anchor">Order 103 · 20 Oct 10:15 · agreed P7 price <strong>20.00</strong> · total <strong>29.00</strong></p>
  </div>
  <p class="history-caption">{advanced ? 'Both accounts remain stored. A1 and A2 stop being the recorded account exactly when A3 and A4 begin. Select 21 October, then change only the recorded time: the answer changes from 20.00 to 22.00.' : 'The shop records the schedule on 21 October at 12:00. A1 ends where A2 begins, at 22 October 00:00. The right edge of A2 is open: no later end has been specified.'} The line marks the selected effective instant; bordered bands and the named assertion identify the selected account and result.</p>
  <details class="history-alt"><summary>Figure as text</summary>
    <p>On 21 October at 12:00 the shop records 20.00 effective before 22 October 00:00, then 22.00 from that instant onwards. At the boundary, only 22.00 applies.</p>
    {advanced && <p>On 24 October at 09:00 it records a correction: the boundary should be 21 October 00:00. For an effective time of 21 October at 12:00, the record at 23 October says 20.00; the record from 24 October at 09:00 says 22.00. Both records give 20.00 at order 103’s time, and neither changes its agreement.</p>}
  </details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { answer, instants, records } from './model.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-price-figure]').forEach(root => {
    const effective = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-effective]')!;
    const recorded = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-recorded]');
    const draw = () => {
      const instant = instants[Number(effective.value)];
      const record = recorded ? records[Number(recorded.value)] : { value: '2026-10-21 12:00:00+00', label: '21 Oct 12:00' };
      const row = answer(instant.value, record.value)[0];
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-marker]').forEach(marker => marker.style.left = `${instant.position}%`);
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-band]').forEach(band => band.classList.toggle('selected-band', band.dataset.band === (recorded?.value || '0')));
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-assertion]').forEach(span => span.classList.toggle('selected-price', Number(span.dataset.assertion) === row.id));
      root.querySelector('[data-price]')!.textContent = row.price;
      root.querySelector('[data-match]')!.textContent = `assertion A${row.id}`;
      root.querySelector('[data-price-explanation]')!.textContent = `Effective at ${instant.label.split(' · ')[0]}, according to the record at ${record.label.split(' · ')[0]}: ${row.price}. ${row.id <= 2 ? 'This account places the price change at 22 Oct 00:00.' : 'The corrected account places the price change at 21 Oct 00:00.'} The end of one period is excluded; the start of the next is included.`;
    };
    effective.addEventListener('change', draw);
    recorded?.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
